    - MAX_BULK_FILES = 50
    - MAX_BULK_BYTES = 200 * 1024 * 1024  (200 MB)
    - _EXT_TO_MIME dict: {".pdf": "application/pdf", ".png": "image/png", ".jpg": "image/jpeg",
      ".jpeg": "image/jpeg", ".docx": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document",
      ".xlsx": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet"}

    Single endpoint: POST /api/compliance/evidence/bulk
    Parameters: zip_file: UploadFile = File(...), manifest: str = Form(...), current_user=Depends(get_current_user)

    Implementation order (two-pass, validate-all-before-commit per BULK-02):

    Pass 0 — manifest parse:
    - json.loads(manifest); check isinstance(items, list) and items non-empty; check each item
      has "filename" and "control_id" keys; raise HTTPException(400) on failure.
    - len(items) > MAX_BULK_FILES → raise HTTPException(400).

    Pass 0b — zip validation:
    - zip_content = await zip_file.read()
    - len(zip_content) > MAX_BULK_BYTES → raise HTTPException(413)
    - not zipfile.is_zipfile(io.BytesIO(zip_content)) → raise HTTPException(400)
    - Open ZipFile; sum(i.file_size for i in zf.infolist()) > MAX_BULK_BYTES → raise HTTPException(400)

    Pass 1 — per-entry validation (inside `with zipfile.ZipFile(...) as zf:` block):
    - errors: list[dict] = []; validated: list[dict] = []
    - For each item in items:
      a. raw_name = item["filename"]; safe_name = os.path.basename(raw_name.replace("\\", "/"))
         If not safe_name or safe_name in (".", ".."): errors.append({"filename": raw_name, "error": "Unsafe filename"}); continue
      b. ext = os.path.splitext(safe_name)[1].lower()
         If ext not in _EVIDENCE_ALLOWED_EXTENSIONS: errors.append; continue
      c. try: entry_bytes = zf.read(raw_name) except KeyError: errors.append({"filename": raw_name, "error": "File not found in zip"}); continue
      d. len(entry_bytes) > 25 * 1024 * 1024: errors.append; continue
      e. not _check_magic(entry_bytes, ext): errors.append; continue
      f. validated.append({"original_name": safe_name, "bytes": entry_bytes, "ext": ext, "control_id": item["control_id"]})
    - if errors: raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail={"errors": errors})

    Pass 2 — commit all (only reached when errors == []):
    - batch_id = uuid.uuid4().hex; timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()
    - db = get_database()
    - For each v in validated:
      - stored_name = f"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{v['ext']}"
      - file_path = os.path.join(UPLOAD_DIR, stored_name)
      - await asyncio.to_thread(_write_binary, file_path, v["bytes"])
      - Build record: id="cev-bulk-{uuid4().hex}", name=v["original_name"], url=f"/static/evidence/{stored_name}",
        type=_EXT_TO_MIME.get(v["ext"], "application/octet-stream"), uploadedAt=timestamp,
        controlId=v["control_id"], tenantId=tenant_id, uploaded_by=uploader,
        description=f"Bulk upload batch {batch_id}", source="manual",
        systemGenerated=False, bulk_batch_id=batch_id
      - await db.control_evidence.insert_one({**record})
      - await _append_coc_entry(db=db, evidence_id=record["id"], tenant_id=tenant_id,
          actor=uploader, action_type="create", snapshot_before=None, snapshot_after=record)
      - record.pop("_id", None); committed.append(record)
    - return {"success": True, "committed": len(committed), "batch_id": batch_id, "evidence": committed}

    Wrap the entire body in try/except HTTPException: raise / except Exception as e: logger.error + raise HTTPException(500).

    File must stay under 200 lines. Do NOT add the endpoint to compliance_evidence_endpoints.py
    (that file is at 495 lines — adding bulk handling would breach the 500-line CLAUDE.md limit).
  </action>
