<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| client → POST /api/compliance/evidence/bulk | Unauthenticated multipart data (zip bytes + manifest JSON string) arrives from browser or API client |
| zip archive interior → server filesystem | Zip entry names and entry bytes are untrusted; path traversal and decompression bomb vectors |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-08-01 | Spoofing | JWT-to-tenantId binding | mitigate | tenantId from getattr(current_user, "tenant_id"), never from request body; get_current_user verifies JWT signature |
| T-08-02 | Tampering | Zip entry path traversal (zip slip) | mitigate | os.path.basename(raw_name.replace("\\", "/")) strips directory components before use as display label; stored filename is uuid4().hex+ext (completely independent of zip entry name) |
| T-08-03 | Tampering | Cross-tenant evidence injection | mitigate | tenantId written into every control_evidence record from JWT, not from manifest |
| T-08-04 | DoS | Zip bomb (decompression bomb) | mitigate | sum(i.file_size for i in zf.infolist()) > MAX_BULK_BYTES (200 MB) guard before any zf.read(); entry count > 50 guard |
| T-08-05 | DoS | Large zip file exhausting disk | mitigate | len(zip_content) > MAX_BULK_BYTES (200 MB) guard before opening ZipFile; per-file 25 MB cap |
| T-08-06 | Spoofing | Polyglot file (valid zip that looks like allowed type) | mitigate | _check_magic() validates first bytes of each entry against declared extension; extension allowlist enforced before magic check |
| T-08-07 | Elevation of Privilege | Non-zip file uploaded (MIME confusion) | mitigate | zipfile.is_zipfile(io.BytesIO(zip_content)) validates the zip container; per-entry extension + magic checks validate contents |
| T-08-08 | Repudiation | Bulk uploads with no audit trail | mitigate | _append_coc_entry called per committed file (fire-and-forget, never raises) |
| T-08-SC | Tampering | npm/pip/cargo installs | accept | No new packages in this phase; entire implementation uses Python stdlib + existing dependencies |
</threat_model>

